  <div class="pf">

  <!-- EMERGENCY LEVELS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Is a Plumbing Emergency on the Wirral?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Some Wirral plumbing problems need an immediate call. Others can wait until morning. Here is how to tell which is which.</p>
      <div class="emerg-levels" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="emerg-level emerg-level--danger">
          <div class="level-header">
            <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🔴</span>
            <div><strong>Call Immediately. Do Not Wait.</strong><span>Stop what you are doing and call now</span></div>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Smell of gas or a hissing sound: call Cadent first on 0800 111 999</strong>, then us</li>
            <li>Burst pipe. Water pouring out</li>
            <li>Flooding. Water rapidly accumulating</li>
            <li>Toilet overflowing and will not stop</li>
            <li>Carbon monoxide alarm going off: get everyone outside, call Cadent on 0800 111 999, then us</li>
            <li>No water to entire property</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="tel:01515580334" class="btn btn-red btn-full" style="margin-top:1rem;color:#ffffff;">Call 0151 558 0334 Now</a>
        </div>
        <div class="emerg-level emerg-level--urgent">
          <div class="level-header">
            <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🟡</span>
            <div><strong>Call Today. Do Not Leave Overnight.</strong><span>Urgent but not immediate danger</span></div>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Major leak. Constant drip or puddle forming</li>
            <li>Toilet leaking at the base or not filling</li>
            <li>No hot water. Boiler not working</li>
            <li>Frozen pipes. Risk of bursting</li>
            <li>Water tank overflow</li>
            <li>Radiator leak</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin:1rem 0 0;font-size:0.93rem;"><a href="tel:01515580334" style="color:#1a3a5c;font-weight:800;">Call 0151 558 0334</a> for advice. A real person answers 24/7.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="emerg-level emerg-level--routine">
          <div class="level-header">
            <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🟢</span>
            <div><strong>Can Wait. Book an Appointment.</strong><span>No immediate danger</span></div>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Dripping tap</li>
            <li>Toilet that keeps running</li>
            <li>Boiler service due</li>
            <li>Radiator not heating well</li>
            <li>Shower pressure low</li>
            <li>General plumbing work</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin:1rem 0 0;font-size:0.93rem;"><a href="/get-started" style="color:#1a3a5c;font-weight:800;">Book a time online</a> that suits you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align:center;margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);">Not sure? Call us and we will tell you straight whether it is an emergency or can wait. <a href="tel:01515580334" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">0151 558 0334</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- PRICING -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Emergency Plumber Wirral. Fixed Hourly Rates.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Fixed prices for the first hour on every Wirral call-out. No hidden charges, parts at cost. The price we quote is the price you pay.</p>

      <div class="pf-pricing-grid">
        <div class="pf-price-card">
          <div class="pf-price-tier">WEEKDAY EMERGENCY</div>
          <div class="pf-price-name">Monday to Friday</div>
          <div class="pf-price-sub">9am to 4pm</div>
          <div class="pf-price-amount">£120<small> first hour</small></div>
          <ul class="pf-price-list">
            <li>Fast Wirral response</li>
            <li>Gas Safe engineer</li>
            <li>Parts at cost only</li>
            <li>No call-out fee</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="tel:01515580334" class="btn btn-navy btn-full">Call Now</a>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-price-card">
          <div class="pf-price-tier">OUT OF HOURS</div>
          <div class="pf-price-name">Evenings and weekends</div>
          <div class="pf-price-sub">Weekdays after 4pm, nights and all weekend</div>
          <div class="pf-price-amount">£150<small> first hour</small></div>
          <ul class="pf-price-list">
            <li>Same fast service</li>
            <li>Gas Safe engineer</li>
            <li>Parts at cost only</li>
            <li>No call-out fee</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="tel:01515580334" class="btn btn-navy btn-full">Call Now</a>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-price-card pf-price-card-featured">
          <div class="pf-price-badge">24/7</div>
          <div class="pf-price-tier">BANK HOLIDAYS</div>
          <div class="pf-price-name">Every bank holiday</div>
          <div class="pf-price-sub">Anytime, 24/7</div>
          <div class="pf-price-amount">£180<small> first hour</small></div>
          <ul class="pf-price-list">
            <li>24/7 Wirral cover</li>
            <li>Emergency priority response</li>
            <li>Gas Safe engineer</li>
            <li>No call-out fee</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="tel:01515580334" class="btn btn-orange btn-full" style="color:#ffffff;">Call Now. We Answer.</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-info-bar" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text);font-weight:600;">Extra time is priced before we carry on. Parts at cost. Written quote before any work begins. Most emergency jobs take 30 to 90 minutes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WIRRAL PROPERTY KNOWLEDGE - UNIQUE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">LOCAL EXPERTISE</span>
      <h2>Wirral Homes. Five Different Areas. Five Different Challenges.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">The Wirral is one of the most varied housing markets in the North West. A Birkenhead shipyard terrace, a Port Sunlight listed home and a Heswall detached are all different. Our engineers know what to look for in each.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">

        <details class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange area-acc" open><summary><span class="area-acc-pc">CH41 CH42</span><strong>Birkenhead and the Cammell Laird Terraces</strong></summary><p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Birkenhead's dense Victorian terraces were built in the late 1800s. They housed Cammell Laird shipyard and dock workers. Many have never had any real plumbing update since. We often find back-to-back layouts and loft tanks feeding the hot water. Old copper pipe is common, and so is the odd run of lead. These homes are also prone to frozen loft pipes in cold snaps where the tank sits above the insulation rather than below it. Our engineers know these layouts well and carry the right parts for Victorian-era systems as standard.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange area-acc"><summary><span class="area-acc-pc">CH44 CH45</span><strong>Wallasey and New Brighton</strong></summary><p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Wallasey and New Brighton are a mix of Edwardian terraces, 1930s semis and post-war homes. Pipework from these eras is often reaching end of life. New Brighton seafront homes face the extra problem of salt air which speeds up rust on outdoor fittings, overflow pipes and any exposed metalwork. We carry replacement outdoor fittings suited to coastal use on every Wirral van.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange area-acc"><summary><span class="area-acc-pc">CH47 CH48</span><strong>Hoylake, West Kirby and the Open Coast</strong></summary><p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Hoylake and West Kirby hold some of the Wirral's most distinct period homes. The streets near Royal Liverpool Golf Club have big detached and semi-detached homes. Many still have their Victorian or Edwardian plumbing layouts. Being right on the coast means outdoor pipework sees harder weather here than anywhere else on the peninsula. In West Kirby we often find outdoor pipes that have failed from salt rust. We also find old loft tanks left in place after a combi boiler swap.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange area-acc"><summary><span class="area-acc-pc">CH62</span><strong>Port Sunlight Listed Homes and Bromborough</strong></summary><p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Port Sunlight is a conservation area with around 900 Grade II listed homes. William Lever built them from 1888 for his soap works staff. These homes are unlike anything else on the Wirral. These homes have half-timbered fronts, original layouts and narrow access. Listed building rules apply, so you need an engineer who knows what is allowed. We work on Port Sunlight homes often. We know what the Local Listed Building Consent Order allows without fresh consent each time. The rest of Bromborough is a mix of post-war estates and newer private builds with modern combi boilers.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange area-acc"><summary><span class="area-acc-pc">CH60 CH64</span><strong>Heswall, Neston and the Dee Estuary Villages</strong></summary><p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Heswall, Neston, Parkgate and Burton hold some of the largest homes on the Wirral. Detached houses with multiple bathrooms, unvented cylinders, pressurised heating and underfloor heating are common in these areas. Faults in these more complex systems need engineers with the right training, including G3 for unvented cylinders. All our engineers hold the training needed to work on these higher-spec systems. When something goes wrong at a Heswall home at midnight, we have the right engineer for the job.</p></details>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CallStrip title="Need a plumber on the Wirral?" text="Emergency or everyday job, call us. We answer 24/7, and there is no call-out fee." />


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Common Emergencies We Fix Across the Wirral</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">The plumbing faults we attend most often across the Wirral peninsula.</p>
      <div class="jobs-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Burst Pipes and Water Through the Ceiling</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">First hour from £120</span><span class="job-time">30 to 90 mins</span></div><p>Common in Birkenhead and Rock Ferry Victorian terraces during cold snaps. Loft tanks and outdoor pipes that have never been insulated are the most common cause. We stop the leak, repair or swap the pipe section and check for hidden damage before we leave.</p>  <a class="job-link" href="/burst-pipe-repair-liverpool"><span>Burst pipe repair</span><span class="lc-arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>No Hot Water and Boiler Breakdown</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">First hour from £120</span><span class="job-time">45 to 120 mins</span></div><p>Old boiler in a Wallasey terrace or a modern one in Heswall, we aim to find and fix the fault on the same visit. Only a Gas Safe registered plumber works on your boiler. Error codes diagnosed before we arrive where possible.</p>  <a class="job-link" href="/no-heating-no-hot-water-liverpool"><span>No heating or hot water</span><span class="lc-arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="job-card job-card--warning"><h3>Gas Leaks</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Call Cadent first</span><span class="job-time">Priority response</span></div><p>If you smell gas, leave the home and call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then call us. Gas Safe registered engineers only.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Major Leaks</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">First hour from £120</span><span class="job-time">20 to 60 mins</span></div><p>Leaking pipes under sinks, radiator leaks, toilet cistern overflows and valve failures. We find the source, stop the leak and repair or swap the part before it causes more water damage to your Wirral home.</p>  <a class="job-link" href="/leak-detection-liverpool"><span>Leak detection</span><span class="lc-arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Heating Failure</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">First hour from £120</span><span class="job-time">60 to 120 mins</span></div><p>Heating failing in the depths of a Wirral winter is a priority call-out for us. We check pump, motor valves, thermostats and pipework.</p>  <a class="job-link" href="/boiler-repair-liverpool"><span>Boiler repair</span><span class="lc-arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- REVIEWS -->
  <section class="pf-section pf-reviews" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom:0.1rem;">What Our Customers Say</h2>
